WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.540
&gt;&gt; WATCHING THIS YEAR'S SHORT
DOCUMENTARY FILMS, I'M REMINDED

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:13.340
BY HOW MUCH IMPACT GOOD
STORYTELLING CAN HAVE AT ANY LENGTH.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.629
"COLETTE" INTRODUCES US TO A

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:22.160
90-YEAR-OLD FRENCH RESISTANCE
FIGHTER, WHOSE THEN 17-YEAR-OLD

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.470
BROTHER, ALSO IN THE RESISTANCE,
WAS SENT TO A GERMAN

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.100
CONCENTRATION CAMP BY THE NAZIS.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.969
“A CONCERTO IS A CONVERSATION”

00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:37.670
IS A GORGEOUS TRIBUTE TO A
GRANDFATHER WHO MADE IT POSSIBLE

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:41.571
FOR HIS FAMILY TO DREAM THE
BIGGEST OF DREAMS.

00:00:43.702 --> 00:00:48.949
“HUNGER WARD” TAKES US INSIDE A
CLINIC IN YEMEN.

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:53.033
THE RESULT IS AS DIZZYING AND
AS DISORIENTING AS WAR ITSELF.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:00.920
EMBEDDED INSIDE THE HONG KONG
PROTESTS FOR "DO NOT SPLIT,"

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.104
THE FILMMAKERS' APPROACH IS 
DEEPLY COLLABORATIVE.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.460
SOPHIA NAHLI ALLISON'S
EXPERIMENTAL DOCUMENTARY "A LOVE

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.340
SONG FOR LATASHA," IS A
MEDITATION ON LIFE AND JOY IN

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.579
THE SOUTH CENTRAL NEIGHBORHOOD
WHERE SHE SPENT HER CHILDHOOD.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.439
AND THE ACADEMY AWARD FOR BEST
DOCUMENTARY SHORT GOES TO --

00:01:32.351 --> 00:01:33.740
“COLETTE”

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.026
ANTHONY GIACCHINO
AND ALICE DOYARD.

00:01:38.026 --> 00:01:42.984
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:12.640
THANK YOU.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.590
TO THE ACADEMY, I HOPE THE
ACTORS IN THE ROOM DON'T MIND

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.340
THAT I HAVE SOMETHING
WRITTEN DOWN HERE

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:23.950
BECAUSE THERE ARE ALL DIFFERENT
KINDS OF PEOPLE IN THE ACADEMY.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.970
TODAY IS COLETTE'S BIRTHDAY.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.480
SHE WAS BORN JUST 
22 DAYS BEFORE

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.820
THE VERY FIRST OSCARS IN 1929.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.220
SO, I IMAGINE IT MUST HAVE BEEN A,
PROBABLY ABOUT A

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.741
CROWD ABOUT THIS BIG, RIGHT?

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:39.860
YOU KNOW?

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:46.790
WHEN WE GOT NOMINATED, SHE TOLD
US THAT, OR SHE REMINDED US THAT

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.530
THE POWER OF DOCUMENTARY
FILMMAKING ENSURED THAT HER

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:55.130
BROTHER, JEAN-PIERRE, WAS,
AS SHE PUT IT, NO LONGER LOST

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.850
IN THE NIGHT AND FOG OF THE
NAZI CONCENTRATION CAMP SYSTEM.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:05.260
AND I WANT TO SAY, I THINK IT'S
THE -- THAT SAME POWER OF THE

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:11.850
DOCUMENTARY STORYTELLING THAT IS
GOING TO ENSURE THAT THE MEMORY,

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:19.770
COURAGE, AND RESILIENCE OF
LATASHA HARLINS, HORACE BOWERS,

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:24.260
THE INNOCENT CHILDREN OF YEMEN,
AND THE PROTESTERS IN HONG KONG

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.260
ARE NOT FORGOTTEN.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.060
I MEAN, THAT'S WHY WE DO THIS.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.850
THAT'S WHY WE MAKE THESE FILMS.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.580
SO THANK YOU.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.820
WE'RE GRATEFUL THAT THESE

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.370
STORIES AND THESE INDIVIDUALS HAVE
BEEN HONORED TONIGHT.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:43.160
AND I ALSO WOULD JUST LIKE TO THANK,
OF COURSE, COLETTE AND LUCIE.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:51.570
I WANT TO THANK OUR AMAZING E.P.,
PETER HIRSCHMANN, AT ELECTRONIC ARTS.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.590
EVERYONE AT ELECTRONIC ARTS,
AND RESPAWN, AND OCULUS

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:58.210
ESPECIALLY VINCE
DUSTY, AND LAURA,

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.980
AND OUR PRODUCERS,
ANNIE SMALL AND AARON MATTHEWS,

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.760
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.760
TO THE GUARDIANS, CHARLIE
PHILLIPS, JESS GORMLEY, AND

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.397
LINDSAY POULTON.

00:04:08.397 --> 00:04:11.660
WE SHARE THIS AWARD WITH YOU.

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:18.900
&gt;&gt; AND I JUST ADD SOMETHING,
THIS AWARD IS A TRIBUTE, AND

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.150
THIS FILM IS A TRIBUTE TO WOMEN
EVERYWHERE IN THE WORLD OF ANY

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:30.199
AGES, THAT -- WHO ARE JOINING
HANDS AND FIGHT FOR JUSTICE.

00:04:30.199 --> 00:04:33.389
[ SPEAKING FRENCH ]

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:35.667
THANK YOU.

